{
  "_comment": "GWY-49 reference data (CLAUDE.md \u00a723): the zero-data-retention capability of every provider the gateway can route to. `zdr` is one of none | default | enterprise, with the meanings and the mapping rule fixed by decisions/ADR-079-zdr-provider-policy-data.md \u00a72: `default` = the provider's own page says the endpoint the gateway calls retains no prompt/response content for ANY purpose (abuse monitoring included) and trains on none, for EVERY account, with no account or model condition; `enterprise` = a documented ZDR mode exists but the CUSTOMER's account must hold it (contract, approval or self-serve setting) -- NOT eligible until slice 2's per-key declaration; `none` = neither, or not read. A row with `verified_at` was read on that date at `policy_url` (the full citation table, with the quoted sentences, is ADR-079 \u00a71); `review_by` is verified_at + 90 days, after which the row must be re-read and re-dated (ADR-079 \u00a74). A row with `verified_at: null` has never been read and ships `none`. A `default`/`enterprise` row MUST carry `policy_url` and `verified_at`; the seed refuses otherwise. Seeded into Neon `provider_capabilities` by apps/web/db/seed.mjs; read by the gateway through its refresher, never per request.",
